{
  "rationale": "Model sensing and motion as separate plants, then use compact specifications to map clear sensing to forward-biased exploration and obstacle sensing to one-shot recovery. Because uncontrollable events are processed before controllable pulses, action states self-loop on non-critical path_clear and only obstacle events preempt when safety requires it. The policy prefers move_forward in clear space, uses directed turns for side obstacles, reserves move_backward for front-obstacle escape, and returns to forward exploration immediately once path_clear is observed.",
  "strategy": [
    "Split plant into a sensor outcome plant and a motion capability plant using only the given events",
    "Use one policy specification with perception states and one-shot action states so each non-perception state enables exactly one controllable action",
    "Bias clear operation to move_forward, allow random_walk only in a dedicated clear-search branch, and keep obstacle recovery conservative and brief",
    "Use rotate_clockwise for left obstacles and rotate_counterclockwise for right obstacles consistently; use move_backward only after obstacle_front",
    "Make all states total on uncontrollable events and let path_clear quickly return recovery states to forward exploration"
  ],
